cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software itself and the
  accompanying research publication (Du, Chen and Chan, Phys. Rev. B 113,
  085134).
title: >-
  vmc_torch: Flexible Variational Monte Carlo for Quantum Many-Body
  Systems with PyTorch
abstract: >-
  A scalable PyTorch implementation of Variational Monte Carlo (VMC) for
  ground-state properties of quantum many-body lattice Hamiltonians, with
  flexible support for Neural Quantum States (NQS), bosonic and fermionic
  Tensor Network States (MPS/PEPS), hybrid neuralized fermionic tensor
  networks (NN-fTNS), and Tensor Network Functions (TNF). Markov chain
  Monte Carlo sampling is distributed via MPI for large-scale HPC
  deployment, and optimization uses PyTorch automatic differentiation
  with Stochastic Reconfiguration and standard machine-learning
  optimizers.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Du
    given-names: Si-Jing
    email: sdu2@caltech.edu
    affiliation: California Institute of Technology
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4737-9308"
version: 0.1.0
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/sjdu10/vmc_torch"
url: "https://github.com/sjdu10/vmc_torch"
# Uncomment and fill in after archiving a GitHub release on Zenodo.
# Use the *concept* DOI so the citation always resolves to the latest
# version.
# doi: 10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX
keywords:
  - variational Monte Carlo
  - tensor networks
  - neural quantum states
  - fermionic tensor networks
  - quantum many-body physics
  - PyTorch
